                  <provenance><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_404">Norwich, Norfolk. Benedictine
                        cathedral priory of Holy Trinity. </orgName><p>Lambeth Palace 192 fols.
                        1--44 and 188 fols. 175--179 were formerly bound together (by Bale?).
                        Sancroft removed five leaves to another volume, but failed to remove with
                        them the leaf still remaining in MS. 192 bearing the scribble "quod R
                        [...]", which shows that it is from the same MS. as MS. 188 fol. 175r on
                        which is written "quod R Gorst" in the same hand.</p><p>A leaf detached from
